  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "gDeap",
      "anchor": "gdeap"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "`gDeap` is the Data Engineering and Analytics Platform capability group. It organizes a simple responsibility chain: consume data from an approved source, process it through governed transformations, and publish it to an approved destination."
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The group is an ownership boundary, not a second import/export engine. File and record import/export contracts remain in `gFramework/nData`; search, messaging, events, databases, and external providers remain owned by their respective modules."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Module Family",
      "anchor": "module-family"
    },
    {
      "kind": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Stage",
        "Owner",
        "Current evidence"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Consume",
          "[dataConsumer](/docs/modules/gdeap/dataconsumer)",
          "External/internal schemas, event handlers, process service, generated schema/API/scenario contracts. Requires flow-specific source and operational qualification."
        ],
        [
          "Process",
          "[dataProcessor](/docs/modules/gdeap/dataprocessor)",
          "Capability scaffold and extension slots; project transformations and behavioral tests are still required."
        ],
        [
          "Publish",
          "[dataPublisher](/docs/modules/gdeap/datapublisher)",
          "Capability scaffold and extension slots; destination providers and behavioral tests are still required."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "End-To-End Contract",
      "anchor": "end-to-end-contract"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Every DEAP flow should define:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "business owner and authoritative source;",
        "input schema/version and source identity;",
        "tenant, classification, retention, and consent/access policy;",
        "message, record, batch, checksum, and idempotency identity;",
        "validation, quarantine, duplicate, ordering, retry, and replay behavior;",
        "deterministic transformations and lineage;",
        "authoritative target and publishing/delivery acknowledgement;",
        "audit, metrics, reconciliation, rollback or compensation, and recovery;",
        "performance limits and positive, negative, boundary, integration, and"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "regression tests."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "What To Avoid",
      "anchor": "what-to-avoid"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Duplicating `nData`, messaging, search, or provider clients inside DEAP.",
        "Accepting arbitrary URLs, credentials, processors, schemas, or destinations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "from request payloads."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Treating a generated CRUD API as a complete ingestion or publishing product.",
        "Losing tenant, source, correlation, lineage, or idempotency context between"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "stages."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Claiming production readiness from scaffold structure alone."
      ]
    },
    {
